Extended Parameter attributes are possible but I can't see a reason why we would ever need them:
```python
class Parameter(wrapt.ObjectProxy):
    .
    .
    .

    def __setattr__(self, name, val):
       try:
            super().__setattr__(name, val)
       except AttributeError:
            super().__setattr__("_self_"+name, val)

    def __getattribute__(self, name):
        try:
             super().__getattribute__(name)
        except AttributeError:
             super().__getattribute__("_self_"+name)

